{
  "lesson_id": "b1-b2_zero_first_conditional_future_time_clauses",
  "level": "B1-B2",
  "title": "Zero and first conditional and future time clauses",
  "description": "Zero Conditional описывает общие истины, правила, routines и predictable results. First Conditional — realistic future possibility.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-B1+-21-RU",
    "lesson_num": 21,
    "title": "Правила: Zero and first conditional and future time clauses",
    "level": "B1-B2",
    "overview": "Zero Conditional описывает общие истины, правила, routines и predictable results. First Conditional — realistic future possibility.",
    "main_rule": "Zero: if/when + Present Simple, Present Simple. First: if + Present Simple, will + V1. Future time clauses with when/as soon as/before/after/until/once use Present rather than will.",
    "form": "Zero: If + Present, Present. First: If + Present, will + V1. Time clause: when/as soon as/etc. + Present.",
    "when_why": "Используем для general truths/predictable results и realistic future conditions/time sequences.",
    "examples": "If you heat ice, it melts. → Если нагреть лёд, он тает.\nWhen the system detects an error, it sends an alert. → Когда система обнаруживает ошибку, она отправляет alert.\nIf it rains, we will stay inside. → Если пойдёт дождь, мы останемся внутри.\nAs soon as she arrives, we'll start. → Как только она придёт, мы начнём.",
    "special_cases": "В future time clause will обычно не ставится: When I finish, I will call you. Result clause может содержать will, modal или imperative.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ When I will finish, I will call you. → ✅ When I finish, I will call you.\n❌ If you heat ice, it will melt. → Для general truth стандартнее If you heat ice, it melts.",
    "dont_confuse": "Zero = general/predictable result. First = realistic future possibility.",
    "quick_summary": "Zero: Present → Present.\nFirst: Present → will.\nFuture time clause → Present, not will."
  },
